UNIT parse_type
LANG js
PRIMARY-SHA256 13ec282f2ac414f28d67d0f388026277b9171b3b207288adedef231a2b912999
SIG parse_type(s: string): object
NOTE named export parse_type
ABI text = string; the result is a fresh plain object per node (k plus the TABLE NODE members), lists are Arrays, a
  record field is a two-element Array [name, node]. A throw (R11) is a thrown Error; the message is not graded. The
  artifact is an ES module that imports nothing.
ENVELOPE as the primary; no widening is claimed.
MECHANISM WHITESPACE (R1) is an explicit test against the four WS characters — never String.prototype.trim and never the
  regex class \s, both of which accept far more. NAME (R7) is the IDENT pin applied at the cursor. Field uniqueness (R9) is
  exact string equality. SAME TYPE (R5) is a structural comparison that ignores union alt order and record field order — a
  set comparison, or an identity string built with the alts' and the fields' strings SORTED (never JSON.stringify of the
  nodes as written, which keeps order). The nesting cap (R10) is a depth counter checked before descending. COVERS (R6) is a recursive
  predicate over two parsed nodes, every clause (a)–(h) tried — it is not a set test on the rendered strings.
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex IDENT = /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*/ CITED R7 and R9 — applied to the text from the cursor; no u or i flag
PROVENANCE rederive@bb8ded84fa50 cli/sir/canon.mjs parseType. Language file re-cut 2026-10-27 with the round-5 primary.
